	&lt;li data-imagepartheight="88.52459016393436" data-imagepartleft="947.5409836065573" data-imageparttop="1780.0819522044699" data-imagepartwidth="127.86885245901635" dir="auto"&gt;στο&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</transcription><translation type="str">&lt;ol dir="auto"&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto" value="1"&gt;To Zhulad, (my) dear brother, and to the&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;assembled members of the household, dutiful greetings (and) homage.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;Moreover, you (pl.) should send hither my share of the . . . And&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto" value="5"&gt;you (sg.) should send me . . . silk(?) (from) which&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;I may make armour(?). And (apart) from this, send hither a donkey-saddle and a bag and a rope(?). And pay one dirham (as) a fee&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto" value="9"&gt;and one dirham (as) a surcharge(?).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;Then I shall buy . . . And (if) I&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;have something more here, I shall send it thither (to you). And to Zhulad and to Zhad-&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto" value="13"&gt;smar, greetings (and) homage from Zhulad. Moreover,&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;in as much as you (pl.) remain in (good) health, (both) yourselves&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;and . . ., you (sg.) should send me (word). So, whatever&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;further news and orders you (pl.) may have,&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;send me (word). And you (sg.) should say thus to Friyak:&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto"&gt;&amp;ldquo;Send one . . . hither from the family(?) on account of Ramin&amp;rdquo;. And say thus to Spring:&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li dir="auto" value="20"&gt;&amp;ldquo;Do not speak at all of the matter of a surcharge(?), because their&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li data-range-end="22" dir="auto"&gt;authorities(?) (are) in agreement and there is no other fee (payable) to them&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</translation><palaeography type="null" /></item><item type="dict"><side type="str">verso</side><openState type="null" /><image type="str">/media/corpus/text_folios__original/jfV.JPG</image><transliteration type="str" /><transcription type="str">&lt;ol dir="auto"&gt;
	&lt;li data-imagepartheight="134.8016304347826" data-imagepartleft="14.315217391304348" data-imageparttop="60.75019834352576" data-imagepartwidth="725.3043478260869" dir="auto" value="23"&gt;ο̣τ̣ο̣μο̣ σ̣τ̣ο̣ρο ταρο φ̣ο̣-&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li data-imagepartheight="141.95923913043478" data-imagepartleft="99.01358695652173" data-imageparttop="113.23932877830836" data-imagepartwidth="607.203804347826" dir="auto"&gt;ϸ̣ταδο μαν̣ο γαοοανζιγ̣ο̣ π̣ι̣-&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li data-imagepartheight="106.1711956521739" data-imagepartleft="87.08423913043478" data-imageparttop="234.9186766043953" data-imagepartwidth="561.8722826086956" dir="auto"&gt;δο πιϸα̣μ̣ω̣σο&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</transcription><translation type="str">&lt;ol dir="auto"&gt;
	&lt;li data-range-end="25" dir="auto" value="23"&gt;And I have sent . . . thither (to you) my dutiful (greetings) with . . .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</translation><palaeography type="null" /></item></folios><personsInText type="list"><item type="dict"><person type="str">Zhulad</person><personNameInText type="null" /><personRoleInText type="str">writer</personRoleInText></item><item type="dict"><person type="str">Zhadsar</person><personNameInText type="null" /><personRoleInText type="null" /></item><item type="dict"><person type="str">Spring</person><personNameInText type="str">Aspring</personNameInText><personRoleInText type="null" /></item><item type="dict"><person type="str">Zhulad</person><personNameInText type="null" /><personRoleInText type="str">addressee</personRoleInText></item></personsInText><publications type="list"><item type="dict"><publication type="str">Sims-Williams, Nicholas. 2007. Bactrian Documents from Northern Afghanistan volume II.</publication><pages type="str">132-3</pages><catalogueNumber type="str">jf</catalogueNumber><details type="str">The IEDC translation and transcription have been taken from this publication</details></item></publications><relatedShelfmarks type="list" /><iedcId type="int">2</iedcId><dateAdded type="str">02/12/2023</dateAdded><dateLastUpdated type="str">07/05/2026</dateLastUpdated><principalEditor type="str">Nicholas Sims-Williams</principalEditor><contributors type="str">Zhan Zhang</contributors><sourceOfData type="str">The transcription and translation have been taken from a previous publication (see Publications)</sourceOfData><permalink type="str">https://www.invisible-east.org/corpus/2/</permalink><imagePermissionStatement type="str">Images of this Text displayed on this web page are provided by Aman ur Rahman Collection. © Aman ur Rahman Collection, All rights reserved. If you wish to reproduce these images please contact Aman ur Rahman Collection.</imagePermissionStatement></item><item type="dict"><uri type="str">IEDC1266</uri><shelfmark type="str">PM 37-33-42 (field no. CT-135/6)</shelfmark><collection type="str">Penn Museum</collection><group ty